{
  "_comment": [
    "PERMANENT manifest for the Flat Category Restructure (epic #196, sub-issue #197).",
    "Do NOT delete or rename this file after the restructure lands -- scripts/check-redirects.mjs",
    "(a later sub-task) reads it forever as the inventory of every old docs route, to verify",
    "public/_redirects covers all of them.",
    "",
    "Consumed by scripts/restructure-docs.mjs (moves files + rewrites links; that script IS",
    "temporary and gets deleted once the cutover is confirmed) and by scripts/check-redirects.mjs.",
    "",
    "See the \"_shape\" key below for the JSON shape of each section (JSON has no comment syntax,",
    "so the shape notes live here instead of inline)."
  ],
  "_shape": {
    "moves": [
      "Array of { old, newCategory }.",
      "`old`: the EN docs-relative path, i.e. relative to src/content/docs/",
      "  (e.g. \"layout/positioning/centering-techniques.mdx\").",
      "`newCategory`: the new top-level (or top-level/deep-article) category directory the file",
      "  lands in (e.g. \"positioning\", or \"design-tokens/tight-token-strategy\" for a deep article).",
      "The basename is unchanged in every move.",
      "New EN path  = `${newCategory}/${basename(old)}`, under src/content/docs/.",
      "New JA path  = `${newCategory}/${basename(old)}`, under src/content/docs-ja/.",
      "Old JA path  = same `old` value, under src/content/docs-ja/ instead of src/content/docs/",
      "  (docs-ja mirrors docs exactly -- verified: 92 articles + 28 index pages per locale).",
      "Old route (EN) = `/docs/${dirname(old)}` + basename-without-extension.",
      "Old route (JA) = `/ja/docs/${dirname(old)}` + basename-without-extension.",
      "New route (EN) = `/docs/${newCategory}` + basename-without-extension.",
      "New route (JA) = `/ja/docs/${newCategory}` + basename-without-extension.",
      "Scope note: this list covers the 92 articles + the 2 deep-article index files",
      "  (design-systems/tight-token-strategy/index.mdx, effects/gradient-techniques/index.mdx)",
      "  -- i.e. every file scripts/restructure-docs.mjs `git mv`s. It deliberately excludes the",
      "  other ~19 old mid-level category index.mdx files (e.g. layout/positioning/index.mdx) --",
      "  those are superseded by freshly authored top-level category index pages in a later wave",
      "  (#199), not moved by this manifest."
    ],
    "deletedRoutes": [
      "Array of { oldCategory, kind }.",
      "Old category directories dissolved entirely by the restructure, with no direct",
      "file-for-file successor -- their `index.mdx` is not in `moves` and the directory ceases",
      "to exist once the cutover lands. Each needs a redirect target chosen in a later wave.",
      "`oldCategory`: docs-relative directory path (e.g. \"layout\", \"layout/specialized\").",
      "`kind`: \"umbrella\" (former header-nav umbrella level whose children were promoted to",
      "  top-level categories) or \"junk-drawer\" (a dissolved leaf category whose children were",
      "  redistributed across other categories).",
      "Old routes needing a redirect: `/docs/${oldCategory}` and `/ja/docs/${oldCategory}`."
    ],
    "newCategoryOrder": [
      "Array of 21 new top-level category directory names, in header-nav display order",
      "(flattening the 8-item/5-group nav from epic #196's target-taxonomy table).",
      "Reference for sidebar_position scope 1 (global, unique positions across all 21 category",
      "index.mdx files) once those files exist -- position = 1-based index into this array."
    ]
  },
